From: AD5X Open OS
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: ingenic: no RDMA start from pan before probe started it

register_framebuffer() makes fbcon pan the screen before probe has run
dpu_ctrl_setup() (display interface, TFT timings, output route) and
filled in the RDMA descriptors. dpu_ctrl_rdma_change() then started the
RDMA right away ("[rdma] last frame [0] still in changing!"). On a cold
X2600 that RDMA hangs as working (DC_ST 0x9), never fetches, cannot be
stopped, and the TFT stage never starts: the panel stays in its
no-signal self-test. It only worked when another driver had left the
TFT running. Only remember the frame until probe has started the RDMA.

diff --git a/module_drivers/drivers/video/fbdev/ingenic/fb_stage_wip/dpu_ctrl.c b/module_drivers/drivers/video/fbdev/ingenic/fb_stage_wip/dpu_ctrl.c
--- a/module_drivers/drivers/video/fbdev/ingenic/fb_stage_wip/dpu_ctrl.c
+++ b/module_drivers/drivers/video/fbdev/ingenic/fb_stage_wip/dpu_ctrl.c
@@ -1469,6 +1469,18 @@
 
 int dpu_ctrl_rdma_change(struct dpu_ctrl *dctrl, int frame)
 {
+	/*
+	 * AD5X: register_framebuffer() pans (fbcon) before probe has run
+	 * dpu_ctrl_setup() and started the RDMA. Starting the RDMA here then
+	 * runs it into an unconfigured DPU: on a cold X2600 it hangs as
+	 * "working" (DC_ST 0x9), never fetches, cannot be stopped, and the
+	 * TFT stage never starts. Only remember the frame until probe's
+	 * dpu_ctrl_rdma_start() has run (work_in_rdma).
+	 */
+	if (!dctrl->work_in_rdma) {
+		dctrl->rdma_last_frame = frame;
+		return 0;
+	}
 	/* TODO: 可能改变的内容，包括格式，大小等。这里只是切换frame, 什么时候真正切换还不一定.*/
 	/*如果此时正处于直通显示, 需要停止直通，切换到rdma通道.*/
 #ifdef CONFIG_ROT_INGENIC
